  <revision rev="13" vrev="13">
    <srcmd5>b7793b1e28ad0ed5b5ef2113a13870c3</srcmd5>
    <version>0.2.5</version>
    <time>1788270425</time>
    <user>anag_factory</user>
    <comment>Add an explicit &quot;Requires: soapy-sdr&quot; to each SoapySDR module subpackage
(soapysdr0.8-3-module-mirisdr, -module-osmosdr, and the bcond'd
-module-freesrp).

The modules link libSoapySDR, so rpm does generate a soname dependency -
but it resolves to libSoapySDR0_8-3, and nothing pulls in the soapy-sdr
package itself, which is what ships SoapySDRUtil. Verified: SoapySDRUtil
is absent from a build root carrying the modules' full dependency closure.
The dependency is added to the module subpackages only, not to
libSoapyOsmoSDR0.

Note this is a deliberate tightening rather than an existing convention:
no SoapySDR plugin currently in Factory carries this dependency (verified
across soapy-rtlsdr, soapy-hackrf, soapy-airspy, soapy-bladerf, soapy-osmo
and soapy-uhd).

Also in this request:
- License corrected to GPL-3.0-or-later; every built source that carries a
  licence header is GPLv3 or later.
- COPYING shipped in the module subpackages.
- %cmake_build instead of a hand-rolled make invocation.

No version change: 0.2.5 is the current upstream tag.</comment>
    <requestid>1374747</requestid>
  </revision>
